{"name":"Rivulet","hex":"#d5dae1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rivulet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small stream; a streamlet; a gill.","Perizoma affinitatum, a geometrid moth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rivulet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stream","blocks":[{"text":"A stream is a continuous body of surface water flowing within the bed and banks of a channel. The channel is a watercourse, although the watercourse may be seasonally or periodically dry. Depending on its location or certain characteristics, a stream may be referred to by a variety of local or regional names. A long, large stream is usually called a river, while a smaller, less voluminous, and more intermittent stream is known as a creek or tributary, among other names."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/%D0%A6%D0%B2%D1%80%D1%86%D0%BA%D0%B0_2_PPRP001.jpg/330px-%D0%A6%D0%B2%D1%80%D1%86%D0%BA%D0%B0_2_PPRP001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stream","wikidata":"Q47521"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg/500px-Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg/1280px-Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg/500px-Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rocky stream in Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APotok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Frozen_stream_En%C3%A4j%C3%A4rvi%2C_Pori.JPG/500px-Frozen_stream_En%C3%A4j%C3%A4rvi%2C_Pori.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_